    "ls|LS16_S9_U_153": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†153 \nANSWERED ON 18.07.2016 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF BUDDHIST SITES \n \n†153. SHRI VINOD KUMAR SONKAR:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether any scheme has been formu lated by the Government \nto develop the underdeveloped Buddhist pilgrimage sites for \nthe purpose of tourism in various parts of the country;  \n(b)  if so, the details of such sites in various States of the country \nincluding Uttar Pradesh;  \n(c)  whether the G overnment has formulated any policy to \npublicise the cultural, heritage and tourist places of the \ncountry at international level;  \n(d)  if so, the achievements made so far in terms of increase in \nnumber of foreign tourists; and  \n(e)  the State-wise funds allocated and expenditure incurred by the \nState Governments for the conservation and beautification of \ncultural and tourist places particularly Buddhist tourist places \nduring the last two years and the current year? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n(a): The Ministry of Tourism has launched the Swadesh Darshan \nscheme in 2014 -15 for integrated development of these based  \ntourist circuits in the country. Buddhist Circuit is one of the thirteen \nthematic circuits identified for development under the scheme. \n \n(b):    Project proposal relating to Buddhist sites in any part of the \ncountry including in the State of Uttar Pradesh are eligible for grant \nof Central Financial Assistance under Buddhist Circuit theme of \nSwadesh Darshan Scheme.  \n\n(c):  The Ministry of Tourism, as part of its on -going activities, \nannually releases print, electronic, online and outdoor media \ncampaigns in the international and domestic markets, under the \nIncredible India brand line , to promote  various tourism destinations \nand products of the country. In addition, a series of promotional \nactivities are undertaken in important and potential tourist \ngenerating markets overseas through the India tourism Offices \nabroad with the objective of showcasing Ind ia’s tourism potential. \nThese  promotional activities include participation in travel fairs and \nexhibitions; organizing road shows, know India seminars & \nworkshops; organizing and supporting Indian food and cultural \nfestivals; publication of brochures; off ering joint advertising and \nbrochure support and inviting media personalities, tour operators \nand opinion makers to visit the country under the Hospitality \nProgrammes of the Ministry. \n \n(d): The number of Foreign Tourist Arrivals in India during 2013, \n2014 and 2015 wer e 6.97 million  (growth of 5.9%) , 7.68 million \n(growth of 10.2%) and 8.03 million (growth of 4.5%), respectively. \n \n(e): List of projects sanctioned for the tourist circuits and \ndestinations during the last two years and the current years is at \nAnnexure. \n \n********* \n\n \nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (e) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. †153 ANSWERED ON 18.07.2016 REGARDING \nDEVELOPMENT OF BUDDHIST SITES. \n \nThe State/UT -wise number of projects sanctioned, amount utilised \nand status under PIDDC Scheme during 2014-15 \n \n2014-15            (Rs. in lakh) \nSl. \nNo. \nName of the \nState \nNo. of \nProject \nAmt. \nSanctioned \nAmt. \nUtilized \nStatus \nOngoing Completed \n1 Andhra \nPradesh \n6 1,862.680 0 6 0 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh \n5 3,631.080 0 5 0 \n3 Assam 3 3,588.450 0 3 0 \n4 Bihar 2 637.060 0 2 0 \n5 Chhattishgarh 2 940.130 0 2 0 \n6 Haryana 0 61.660 0 0 0 \n7 Jammu & \nKashmir \n1 732.500 0 1 0 \n8 Karnataka 1 5,124.790 0 1 0 \n9 Madhya \nPradesh \n3 3,657.540 60.000 3 0 \n10 Manipur 5 14,877.210 0 5 0 \n11 Mizoram 1 4,829.690 241.485 1 0 \n12 Nagaland 9 6,074.300 1,460.520 9 0 \n13 Odisha 2 1,488.340 0 2 0 \n14 Punjab 1 4,796.980 0 1 0 \n15 Puducherry 0 97.380 0 0 0 \n16 Rajashthan 0 109.930 0 0 0 \n17 Sikki