    "ls|LS16_S9_U_179": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.179 \nANSWERED ON 18.07.2016 \n \nINITIATIVE TO BOOST TOURISM IN NEPAL \n \n179.  SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government ha s taken any measures to help \nNepal to boost tourism after the last year's earthquake and if \nso, the details thereof;  \n(b)  whether the Government plans to introduce more means of \ntransport for tourists to travel to Nepal; and  \n(c)  if so, the details there of along with the action taken by the \nGovernment in this regard? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a) to (c): The Ministry of Tourism has already signed a \nMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Government of N epal for \ncooperation in the field of Tourism. The MoU envisages cooperation \nin the fields of -  \n \ni) Exchange of information and data related to tourism. \nii) Cooperation between tourism stakeholders including \nhotels & tour operators. \niii) Exchange programme s for cooperation in Human \nResource Development. \niv) Investment in the Tourism and Hospitality sector. \nv) Exchange of visits of Tour Operators/Media/Opinion \nMakers for promotion of two way tourism. \nvi) Exchange of experience in the areas of promotion, \nmarketing, destination development and management. \nvii) ���������������������������� ������ �������������� ������������������������������������ ������ ���������� ����������������\ncountry. \nviii)  Promotion of safe, honourable and sustainable tourism. \n********* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_180": "O.I.H.\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 180\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28.07.2016\nWAGE ARREARS UNDER MGNREGS\n*180. SHRI NANA PATOLE:\nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) the funds released to the States under Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment\nGuarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) during 2015-16 and 2016-17, State/UT-wise;\n(b) the details of the outstanding wages for the year 2015 -16 and the funds allocated for\nnew works or activities for the year 2016-17, State/UT-wise;\n(c) whether the expenditure incurred on various relief schemes in drought affected areas\nby the State Gov ernments was also included in the allocated funds, and if so, the\ndetails thereof;\n(d) the details of the expenditure incurred by the States for drought relief during 2015 -16\nand 2016-17, and the time by which these expenditure are likely to be reimbur sed by\nthe Union Government under MGNREGS; and\n(e) the details of the measures taken by the Government to curb the irregularities which\nhave come to its notice under MGNREGS?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nStatement in reply to Parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 180 for 28.07.2016\n(a): State-UT-wise details of amount released under the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural\nEmployment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) during 2015 -16 and 2016 -17 is indicated\nin Annexure-I.\n(b): State/UT-wise details of the pending wage liability for the year 2015 -16 is given in\nAnnexure-II. Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGN REGA) is a\ndemand driven programmes hence no State/UT - wise allocation of fund is made. The Central\nfunds are released to the States/UTs on the basis of agreed to Labour Budgets and taking into\nconsideration the performance and the pace of utilization of available funds. State-UT-wise details\nof amount released for implementation of MGNREGA including for undertaking new works or\nactivities for the year 2016-17 is indicated in Annexure-I.\n(c): No, Madam.\n(d): Funds for programme implementation are released to the States including drought affected\nStates as per the agreed to Labour Budget and shelf of projects. Details of expenditure incurred\nunder the MGNREGS on the drought affected States during 2015 -16 and 2016 -17 is indicated\nin Annexure-III.\n(e): The M inistry, under MGNREGA receives complaints of irregularities including non -\npayment of wages etc. in many State/UTs. Since the responsibility of implementation of\nMGNREGA is vested with the State Governments, all complaints received in the Ministry are\nforwarded to the concerned State Governments for taking appropriate action including\ninvestigation, as per law. Detailed instructions by way of Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for\ndealing with complaints have also been issued to all States/UTs.\n*****\n\nAnnexure-I referred in reply to part s (a&b) of Lok Sabha Starred\nQuestion No. 180 dated 28.07.2016\n(Rs. In lakh)\nStates/UTs wise release position of MGNREGA (2015-16 and 2016-17 )\nS. No States 2015-16 2016-17 (22.7.16)\n1 Andhra Pradesh 307380.330 338835.08\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 4395.100 9525.22\n3 Assam 87830.060 49739.52\n4 Bihar 102412.260 80378.98\n5 Chhattisgarh 106341.300 133272.13\n6 Gujarat 30598.720 43199.86\n7 Haryana 12470.720 6445.17\n8 Himachal Pradesh 39610.320 26172.66\n9 Jammu & Kashmir 55801.830 44887.03\n10 Jharkhand 97879.900 95645.56\n11 Karnataka 99155.270 126971.45\n12 Kerala 152633.877 89007.95\n13 Madhya Pradesh 236732.200 204440.40\n14 Maharashtra 123834.730 112850.70\n15 Manipur 25532.290 27723.41\n16 Meghalaya 22182.560 55560.99\n17 Mizoram 28517.360 1992.14\n18 Nagaland 26665.950 50152.80\n19 Odisha 147941.050 114656.75\n20 Punjab 24533.370 27511.92\n21 Rajasthan 269583.230 301819.00\n22 Sikkim 8623.440 5953.46\n23 Tamil Nadu 