    "ls|LS16_S9_U_197": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 197\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2016\n \n \nPROMOTION OF AGRO\n-\nBASED  MSME\n \n \n197.\n \nSHRI A.T. NANA PATIL:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to promote establishment of new \"Micro, Small \nand Medium Enterprises\" (MSMEs) in agro based industries and food processing \nindustries in Maha\nrashtra; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof alongwith the funds allocated and utilized  for the purpose \nduring each of the last three years and the current year; \n \n(c) whether the Government also proposes to establish 'Skill Development Training \nInstitute' or \n'Entrepreneurship Training and Development Institute' in Maharashtra to \npromote establishment of new  units; and \n \n(d) if so, the details and the location thereof along with the time by which the it is \nlikely to be established?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN T\nHE MINISTRY OF\n \n  \nMICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH)\n \n \n(\na)&(b)\n:  Government in the Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises \n(MSME) has two schemes namely, Prime Minister’s Employment Generation \nProgramme\n \n(PMEGP) and Scheme of Fund for Regeneration of Traditional Industries \n(SFURTI) which provides assistance for setting up of individual enterprises as well as \ncluster based enterprises in the non\n-\nfarm sector by helping traditional artisans and \nunemployed yo\nuth.  Ministry has also launched A Scheme for Promotion of \nInnovation, Rural Industry and Entrepreneurship (ASPIRE) which provides for setting \nup of incubation centres in agro\n-\nbased industry for innovation and enterprise creation \nin micro and small scale i\nndustry including food processing.  Funds utilized and \nemployment generated during each of the last three years under PMEGP Scheme \nincluding agro\n-\nbased Industry in the country including the state of Maharashtra is \nplaced at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n. \n \n \n(\nc\n):\n \nPresently the\nre is no such proposal.    \n \n \n(d\n):\n \nDoes not arise.\n \n* * *\n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \nAnnexure\n-\nI referred to in reply to parts (a)&(b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 197 for answer on 18.07.2016\n \n \nState/UT\n-\nwise details of Margin money utilized and Employment generated under \nPMEGP scheme \n \nSl.\nNo\n \nState/UT\n \nEmployment (in persons)\n \nMargin Money Utilized \n(Rs.in lakhs)\n \n2013\n-\n14\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n2016\n-\n17\n#\n \n2013\n-\n14\n \n2014\n-\n15\n \n2015\n-\n16\n \n2016\n-\n17\n#\n \n1.\n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n877\n \n936\n \n12115\n \n0\n \n264.02\n \n300.99\n \n3781.19\n \n0\n \n2.\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n495\n \n602\n \n5134\n \n836\n \n174.05\n \n229.06\n \n1767.26\n \n359.63\n \n3.\n \nPunjab\n \n1585\n \n1001\n \n7762\n \n3758\n \n621.77\n \n520.41\n \n2902.97\n \n1000.23\n \n4.\n \nU.T. Chandigarh\n \n37\n \n28\n \n323\n \n101\n \n5.14\n \n15.5\n \n87.72\n \n33.38\n \n5.\n \nHaryana\n \n957\n \n1058\n \n7232\n \n980\n \n340.83\n \n470.77\n \n3112.09\n \n457.26\n \n6.\n \nDelhi\n \n32\n \n64\n \n2048\n \n68\n \n5.13\n \n6.22\n \n254.05\n \n18.64\n \n7.\n \nRajasthan\n \n1849\n \n2325\n \n14537\n \n155\n \n599\n \n752.1\n \n4384.07\n \n123.70\n \n8.\n \nUttarakhand\n \n1705\n \n1360\n \n6161\n \n623\n \n551.05\n \n374.15\n \n1740.86\n \n194.84\n \n9.\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n18175\n \n14060\n \n43059\n \n18796\n \n6170.51\n \n5697.1\n \n14456.87\n \n6304.69\n \n10.\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n878\n \n1265\n \n9496\n \n1338\n \n339.32\n \n496.82\n \n2829.38\n \n624.88\n \n11.\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n4578\n \n5556\n \n16497\n \n3104\n \n2316.73\n \n2726.18\n \n8117.17\n \n1741.26\n \n12.\n \nSikkim\n \n39\n \n14\n \n397\n \n6\n \n19.8\n \n10.99\n \n186.11\n \n2.49\n \n13.\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n805\n \n227\n \n104\n \n376\n \n109.04\n \n90.51\n 